---
// Procedural page: describes what happens after a visitor acts. It restates
// no framework definitions; it links to the canonical page instead. Exempt
// from the direct-answer block and evidenceLevel, not exempt from the
// Canonical Link Rule or the writing rules. See CLAUDE.md.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://uncrashableholdings.com');
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: site.toString() },
  { name: 'Contact', url: new URL('/contact', site).toString() },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Start a conversation with Uncrashable Holdings. Send a message, then take the Invisible Fragility Index that fits your situation."
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <h1>Start a Conversation</h1>

  <p>
    Use the form below to reach Uncrashable Holdings. Your message arrives as you send it, and you can complete an Index afterward if it fits.
  </p>

  <div class="form-frame">
    <iframe
      src="https://tally.so/embed/je6X8Y?hideTitle=1&transparentBackground=1"
      title="Contact form: start a conversation with Uncrashable Holdings"
      loading="lazy"
      width="100%"
      height="620"
    ></iframe>
  </div>
  <p class="fallback">
    The form not loading? <a href="https://tally.so/r/je6X8Y" rel="noopener">Open it in its own page</a>.
    Please do not include account numbers, identification numbers, or sensitive medical or financial details in your message.
  </p>

  <h2>After You Send Your Message</h2>

  <p>
    If your question comes from a continuity concern, the next step is the <a href="/diagnostics/ifi">Invisible Fragility Index</a> that fits your situation. It lets you evaluate your own exposure at your own pace.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://tally.so/r/vG1xeD" rel="noopener">Household Invisible Fragility Index</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://tally.so/r/7Rz9R0" rel="noopener">Business Owner Invisible Fragility Index</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://tally.so/r/A7yMVy" rel="noopener">Nonprofit Invisible Fragility Index</a></li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    What happens next depends on what the Index finds. When the findings concentrate in one or two areas, a scoped <a href="/continuity-architecture">Continuity Architecture</a> engagement may be the direct next step. When dependencies interact across several pillars, the <a href="/diagnostics/continuity-stress-test">Continuity Stress Test</a> comes first, to understand why before deciding what to build.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you are not sure where to begin, the <a href="/diagnostics/continuity-scan">Continuity Scan</a> is the first conversation. Reaching out is not a pitch. It is a conversation about what you are seeing, and what, if anything, is worth doing about it.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* The Tally form renders dark text on a transparent background. On the
     charcoal page that text is unreadable, so the form sits on a cream panel. */
  .form-frame { margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; background: var(--cream); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; }
  .form-frame iframe { border: 0; display: block; width: 100%; background: transparent; }
  .fallback { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--cream-dim); }
  h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>
